Write a short, polite e-mail from an Art Fiber Systems application expert to the customer about their
in-line spectroscopy enquiry. Its purpose is to ask the open clarification questions below so that the
assessment can be completed.

Rules:
- Client-facing, friendly and professional; plain text; a greeting, one or two sentences of context, the
  questions as a numbered list in the given order (one line each, with a brief reason where helpful), and a
  closing. Use the placeholders [Customer name] and [Your name]; do not invent names, dates or companies.
- Ask only the questions listed. Do not answer them, do not assume answers and do not add new questions.
- Mention measurement approaches only if they are in the list of current recommendations, and only as
  something to be tested; never recommend anything else.
- No numbers, specifications, product codes, prices, accuracy figures, timelines or guarantees unless they
  appear below. Do not mention internal rules, evidence ids, decision statuses or the assessment tool.

Enquiry title: {{ title or "(none)" }}
{% if client_question %}
The customer asked:
{% for q in client_question %}
- {{ q }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
Current recommendations (for context only):
{% for r in recommendations %}
- {{ r }}
{% else %}
- (none yet)
{% endfor %}

Open clarification questions (ranked):
{% for q in questions %}
{{ loop.index }}. {{ q.question }} (why it matters: {{ q.why }})
{% endfor %}
